# =============================================================================
#  Repository root.
# =============================================================================
#  The per-app .gitignore files cover backend/ and frontend/. This one exists
#  for the Docker stack, which introduced a root-level .env.
# =============================================================================

#  The compose stack's environment: Partner API token, admin password, JWT
# secret. `.env.example` is the file that belongs in version control.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.DS_Store

# ANCHORED. Unanchored, `docs/` matches at every depth — it was silently
# swallowing `backend/docs/` including the `.gitkeep` placed there to make the
# directory trackable, and would have taken any future `frontend/docs/` or
# `.github/docs/` with it. Each ignored docs tree is now named on purpose.
/docs/
backend/docs/

# ── Credential files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not hypothetical: `.env.example` invites an operator to point
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS at a service-account key on disk, and the
# obvious place to put it is right here. Without these lines a file named
# `gcp-key.json` in this directory is TRACKED, and a key that reaches a public
# repository is compromised the moment it is pushed — rotating it is the only
# remedy, and history rewriting does not help once it has been fetched.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*-key.json
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
secret/
secrets/

# SSH / GPG private keys. `*.key` and `*.pem` above miss the conventional
# OpenSSH filenames, which carry no extension at all.
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*.ppk
*.jks
*.keystore
.npmrc
.netrc
.pgpass

# Vendored working notes and third-party material. Excluded from publication
# deliberately, not incidentally: this lived only in .git/info/exclude, which is
# machine-local and travels with no clone — so any other checkout was one
# `git add -A` away from publishing it.
AlgoDocs/

# Google service-account keys, by FILENAME rather than by location.
# Google's own download name is <project-id>-<12 hex>.json, which matches none
# of the *-key.json / *service-account*.json / *credentials*.json rules above.
# Until now the only thing standing between a live BigQuery credential and a
# `git add -A` was the `secret/` DIRECTORY rule in backend/.gitignore — one
# `mv`, or one operator who downloads the key somewhere else, and it ships.
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].json
adc.json
sa.json
gha-creds-*.json
.gcloud/
.config/gcloud/

# Editor backups. `.env~` is a byte-for-byte copy of `.env` — which holds the
# Partner API token, the admin password and the JWT signing key. These were
# ignored ONLY by the machine-local global excludes, which travel with no clone,
# so every contributor was unprotected. Same trap the AlgoDocs note above records.
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.envrc
